PUBLIC RESPONSE: {C}

The ESA requires employers with 25+ employees on January 1 of a given year to maintain (and distribute) written policies on disconnecting from work and electronic monitoring. Distribution of any new or updated policy must occur within 30 days.  

- A, D and E each had fewer than 25 employees on both 1 Jan 2022 and 1 Jan 2023, so no policy obligation existed.  
- B likewise fell below the threshold (23 employees) and therefore was under no statutory duty to create or circulate the policies.  
- C met the 25-employee threshold and therefore was required to keep both policies current and to furnish every revised version to staff inside the 30-day window. Updating monthly while distributing only quarterly necessarily produces late deliveries, violating the distribution rule.  

Hence only C is out of compliance as of 2 Jan 2023.}

